References: <006501c703f0$3e081560$0100000a@KARENSLAPTOP>
Message-ID: <455332A2.10202@med.umich.edu>

Hi Karen,

Karen Vranizan wrote:
> How would one get an overall F test (moderated) and p value for a one-way anova with 4 groups?  

After you have fit your model and done the eBayes() step, the resulting 
MArrayLM object will contain the F-statistic and p-value, which can be 
extracted. Say your MArrayLM object is called fit2. Then fit2$F will 
give you the F-stat and fit2$F.p.value will give you the unadjusted p-value.

Best,

Jim


